implementation_decision:
Keep the manual path (download, share and copy-caption) as the only TikTok path Studio Assistant ships. Do not build a direct TikTok video.upload or inbox integration under Studio Assistant's own developer app.

Correct the stated reason in docs/research/decisions-summary.md. On TikTok's official text, the inbox path is not clearly blocked by the SELF_ONLY or private-account rules. Those rules and their error code are documented only for Direct Post, and the inbox init call takes no privacy setting at all. The real blocker comes earlier, at app review. The App Review Guidelines say 'Apps must not be for private or personal use'. That bar applies to the review that grants video.upload, separately from the Direct Post audit's 'utility tool ... account(s) you or your team manages' clause. So 'passed app review but not the Direct Post audit' is not a realistic state for a single-barber, own-account app.

Even if inbox drafts worked:
- the owner would probably still paste the caption, because video inbox uploads carry no post_info;
- only 5 unfinished drafts are allowed per 24 h.
The saving over today's manual flow is therefore small.

Optional, time-boxed research spike only (no production code, behind no user-facing feature): create a TikTok for Developers sandbox, add the owner's TikTok Business Account as a target user, and try POST /v2/post/publish/inbox/video/init/ with FILE_UPLOAD. Record in docs/research:
- whether the sandbox grants video.upload;
- whether init returns SEND_TO_USER_INBOX;
- whether the draft can be posted with visibility 'Everyone';
- whether Add Sound shows Commercial Sounds.
A positive result still does not license shipping on a sandbox or skipping app review.

If the owner wants renders to land in TikTok drafts, take the existing Stage C route instead: an already audited provider behind a feature flag with an honest 'needs setup' state. Candidates are Zernio with draft: true, Buffer, or IFTTT's 'Upload video draft' action fed a short-lived signed export URL. In that case, extend the publishing status model with 'sent-to-TikTok-drafts' (provider-confirmed) before the owner's manual 'posted' confirmation.
